<SiteLayout title="Verification" description="Identity, adulthood and photo checks answer different questions. Swoovr\u2019s approach is to explain the difference." eyebrow="Trust, explained" heading="A check should mean something clear." intro="Identity, adulthood and photo checks answer different questions. Swoovr\u2019s approach is to explain the difference.">
<section class="editorial-split"><h2>Clear meaning.<br />No blanket promises.</h2><div><p>Our product plan includes adulthood and identity checks before live discovery and contact. We’re assessing appropriate verification methods and alternatives, including how people can get help when a check doesn’t work for them.</p><p>The final methods, providers and eligibility rules will be explained before people are asked to use them. Signing up for website updates or beta interest is not an identity check.</p></div></section><section class="reading-section"><h2>Different checks, different jobs</h2><dl class="definitions"><dt>Identity and adulthood</dt><dd>Intended to establish that a person meets the adult eligibility requirements and has completed the stated identity process. A legal name should not become a public profile requirement by default.</dd><dt>Photo and image signals</dt><dd>A photo check or duplicated-image signal can help investigate an inconsistency. It does not prove someone owns a photograph or establish their intentions.</dd><dt>Account sign-in</dt><dd>Signing in with an email or a social provider is about access to an account. It should not be presented as proof of identity or as a substitute for a separate verification process.</dd></dl></section><section class="editorial-split"><h2>Less information.<br />A clearer purpose.</h2><div><p>Our design preference is to retain the minimum verification result needed, rather than keeping copies of raw identity documents by default. Provider handling, retention and alternatives must be explained alongside the actual process.</p><p>Please don’t send ID, selfies or verification documents through this website’s signup or contact forms. Those forms are for conversations with the team.</p><p>A completed check cannot guarantee someone’s behaviour, eliminate fraud or replace your own boundaries.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Ask a verification question ↗</a></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
